1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birger Sjöström writes: "Anders Mårtensson, born in 1756, was the one who would come to Åkullsjön number seven; it would later become the village Åsjön. The farm was on the north side of the lake. Where life went o
2 CONC n and Anders Mårtensson with his wife Catharina had four children: Martin, born in 1789, Stina Cajsa, born in 1793, Anders, born in 1797, Nils, born in 1800.
2 CONT
2 CONT "When a general land partition reform (the 'storskifte' land reform) was implemented all
2 CONT over Sweden Åsjön became a separate village and no longer a part of Åkullsjön. This was
2 CONT performed in 1796. In 1800 Anders did inspect more land on the south side of the lake.
2 CONT It would be necessary because the family was growing. The wife Catharina's two sons
2 CONT from previous marriage sold their rights to the homestead to their stepfather Anders
2 CONT when they came of age. That was in 1809. At that time, Anders was sole owner of Åsjön.
2 CONT
2 CONT "The Accident
2 CONT
2 CONT "Anders Mårtensson, born in 1756, died in 1814 in an accident in the forest. “Death of
2 CONT striking tree, 59 years old”, it is written in the church register. It was, according to a
2 CONT narrator, when he cut lumber to new buildings on the south side of the lake at the so-­-
2 CONT called Västeråkern (West in the field). In that place there had already been a small
2 CONT pasture chalet. I understand that there had been two shacks in Åsjön. One shack was on
2 CONT the south side of the lake and the other on the north side. The south was the part of the
2 CONT homestead that the son Mårten Andersson has already received over 1811 and just
2 CONT moved into. Here Anders had previously built a new farm and a barn with his sons. The
2 CONT farm was later called Anders Mårtensson's cabin. Now he would build more timber
2 CONT buildings, including a barn and a granary. For these buildings, he needed heavy timber
2 CONT and it would now be his death. The wife Chatarina Larsdotter died in 1817, '62 years
2 CONT old, gout and toothache'.
2 CONT
2 CONT "The kids (except his son Mårten who had his own housing) helped out after the death of their
2 CONT father to take care of their father's farm on the north side of the lake. In 1819 the
2 CONT sons cast lots for the right of possession and son Anders Andersson, born in 1797, then won. He thus became the owner of half of the village Åsjön."
2 CONT
2 CONT See Birger's Åsjön article for a picture of "Overgrown foundations to the house belonging to the older Anders Mårtensson (born in 1756) in Åsjön."
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT From A History of the Family Mårtensson in Åsjön, by Birger Sjöström (2015), https://www.familysearch.org/memories/memory/194212734
2 CONT ------------------------------------
