1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "His [Nils Anderson's] sister *Stina Cajsa*, born in 1793, married to the soldier Olof Sjöman and they toke over the settlement Frodtjärnbäck. The settlement had been approved by the authorities in 1798 and was own
2 CONC ed by Anders Mårtensson. From 1811 one half of the settlement was assigned to his son Mårten Andersson. Later, the father also transferred the other half to Mårten. So it was until 1818. Then Mårten Andersson transferred the settl
2 CONC ement to Olof Sjöman who in 1817 married to Mårten's sister Stina Cajsa. The couple had three children of whom two died early. Olof himself died in 1821. Stina Cajsa remarried in 1822 to the farmhand Anders Jonsson, born 1794. And
2 CONC ers and Stina Cajsa then became permanent residents in Frodtjärnbäck for the rest of their lives."
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources listed at
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/KJCR-XZX
