1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birger Sjöström writes: "Anders Andersson was born in 1797 had in 1819 become owner of half of the village Åsjön [after he and his brothers cast lots for the right of possession of their father's farm]. He was the 
2 CONC owner of the farm in just one year before he sold it. He came, however, to return in 1824 when he bought back the farm. In 1831 Anders sold once again his farm in Åsjön and moved out. In 1842 he bought back his family farm. He cam
2 CONC e to stay here until 1845, when he sold the estate to the former soldier Johan Strid and moved to Åkullsjön where he was living the rest of his life. The homestead in Åsjön soon came to be divided and become two."
2 CONT
2 CONT From "A History of the Family Mårtensson in Åsjön," by Birger Sjöström (2015), https://www.familysearch.org/memories/memory/194212734
