1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Kråken 20 person 193501
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Birger Sjöström writes: After Nil's father dies "The kids (except Mårten who had his own housing) helped out after the death of their father to take care of their father's farm on the north side of the lake. In 1819 the sons cast 
2 CONC lots for the right of possession and son Anders Andersson, born in 1797, and then won. He thus became the owner of half of the village Åsjön.
2 CONT "Nils Andersson, born in 1800, the loser in the lottery draw, became a farmhand on the farm and in other places. In 1830 he moved to Botsmark, Sävar parish, where he was married in 1833 and had his own farm on Boberget, Botsmark. 
2 CONC His son Martin Nilsson, born in 1844, moved to Bygdsiljum and became the ancestor of the owners of the large sawmill industry Martinson Wood, who now keeps on conquering the world."
2 CONT (From "A history of the family Mårtensson in Åsjön," Birger Sjöström (2015))
