1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birger Sjöström writes: "In 1859 Anders brother Per Mårtensson, born in 1838, took over his father's part of the homestead. Per married in 1860 to a sister of the brother's wife. It was Magdalena Johanna Johansdott
2 CONC er Strid, born in 1827. Per and Magdalena Johanna had six children between 1860 and 1870. They came to live on the family farm until 1869 when they moved to the nearby Andersliden. Later, in 1873, they moved to Krokbäck. The move 
2 CONC was due to the severe famine years of 1866-1869, who had been devastating on the family finances. Almost no blade of grass grew on the ground for several summers. The village Åsjön was harder hit than the surrounding villages. Per
2 CONC  had also got into trouble with the law. He was sentenced in 1867 to six months imprisonment with hard labor for counterfeiting. 1869 Per sold his farm to the iron master Erik Häggström in Dalkarlså. This man later also bought up 
2 CONC two other homesteads in Åsjön. Per Mårtensson used to be called "Per-Mårtsa".
2 CONT
2 CONT "I should also mention that Per Mårtensson was known as a reliable man and an incredibly talented worker. After being forced to sell his farm in Åsjön he became a form of farm laborer in the nearby villages. It has been told that 
2 CONC he was a talented settler. He had no large earnings but received daily food for himself and his family. The family was now very poor and there are stories about how kids barely had clothes on the body. When someone came to visit, 
2 CONC they ran and hid themselves. In 1882, Per Mårtensson moved to Grundsunda parish, Ångermanland. There, Per worked at Husum sawmill. There he was a good worker. Now he had at least regular income."
2 CONT
2 CONT Allan Anderson notes:
2 CONT Uncle to my grandpa Anderson, brother to my great grandpa Anders Mårtensson.
2 CONT Shown w/parents: thekids Anders Pehr MariaCharlotta Brita Ingrid Mag+Eva A1:11A.199 (1838-41).
2 CONT was Bonde i Åsjön, Nybyggare i Krokbäcken och Arbetare.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dömd 1867 till 6 månaders straffarbete för förfalskning (Sentenced in 1867 to 6 months hard-work for counterfeiting).
2 CONT
2 CONT Shown as widower with 6 kids age 12 up at Krokbäcken AI:15C.696 (1874-84) Bygdeå; After death of his wife #1 Magdalena Johanna Strid of feber 2/1/1882 the family moves on 23 Oct 1882 (same date as other Strid dotter now a widow re
2 CONC locates) from Krokbäcken, Bygdeå to Godemersta Gideabacka in Grundsunda, Vasternorrlands=(Y), where on 11/25/1882 per A1:8A.51 widower Per w/half dozen kids re-marries to a very recently (11/1/1881) widowed Karolina Charlotta Stri
2 CONC d; there shown as torpare w/ son Karl Johan Persson in Dombäcksön, Grundsunda (Y), the northernmost coastal part of Vasternorrlands, nearest to Umeå.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family shown at Dombäcksön, Grunsunda A1:9A.89 (1885-94), as Per's kids flee nest.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1890 Census: Mårtensson, Pehr Torpare b.1838 i Bygdeå (Västerbottens län,
2 CONT Man, married (father) i Dombäcksön Grundsunda (Västernorrlands län, Ångermanland) Place of birth (original source): Bygdeå.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Missing book about Per Mårtensson
2 CONT A message by "Elisabeth Johansson (Eljo)" posted in 2003 on a Swedish bulletin board (link is dead) mentions "My grandfather's cousin Esther Lundström In her book about Per Mårtensson (Anders brother) ". I have not located the boo
2 CONC k (genealogy?) or the poster on aforum.genealogi.se
2 CONT Reply to broken link at: https://forum.rotter.se/index.php?topic=136685.msg1400404#msg1400404
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT Birger Sjöström, A History of the Family Mårtensson in Åsjön," (2015) on familysearch memories.
